<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Metadata for the now-playing widget, read by the launcher before any of our
  code runs.

  ## Sizes

  The design pack draws the same card at two widths: 350dp on the phone
  (design/html/15-Widget.html, inside a 390dp screen with 20dp gutters) and
  420dp on the tablet (design/html/18-TabletWidget.html). Its internals are
  identical at both — 14dp padding, a 64dp cover, the transport, the position
  row — so one fluid composition serves both artboards and there is no
  tablet-only layout to maintain. NowPlayingWidget uses SizeMode.Exact and
  reads the real size from LocalSize, so the card fits whatever cell count the
  launcher actually gives it rather than snapping to a breakpoint.

  The numbers below are stated in the launcher's own terms. The conventional
  translation from grid cells to dp is `70 * n - 30`:

    * minWidth 250dp  = 4 columns. The card needs 64 (cover) + 12 + 124
      (transport) + 28 (padding) = 228dp before a single character of the title
      fits, so anything narrower cannot draw the design at all.
    * minHeight 110dp = 2 rows. The drawn card is 14 + 64 + 12 + 14 + 14 = 118dp
      tall with the position row, and the position row is the part that drops
      first when it does not fit.
    * targetCellWidth/Height say the same thing to Android 12 and later, which
      places by cell count rather than by dp.
    * maxResizeWidth is generous because a tablet home screen is wide and the
      card is happy to stretch; maxResizeHeight is not, because nothing in the
      design grows vertically and a 300dp-tall now-playing card would just be
      empty space.

  ## updatePeriodMillis is 0, deliberately

  The platform clamps this to 30 minutes and wakes the device to honour it,
  which would be both far too slow for a transport and a pointless battery cost
  for a widget whose content only changes when playback does. Updates are
  pushed instead: while the app's process is alive the Glance session recomposes
  from PlaybackController's flows, and every transport tap republishes. See
  NowPlayingWidget's KDoc, "How state reaches the launcher".

  ## initialLayout

  glance_default_loading_layout ships inside glance-appwidget and is what the
  launcher shows for the few milliseconds between the widget being dropped and
  the first composition arriving. Writing our own would mean maintaining a
  second, static copy of the card for a frame nobody reads.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/widget_now_playing_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="110dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="640dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="170dp"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_now_playing_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
